   "install": {
    "title": "Quick start",
    "html": "<p>A few options to get <code>llama.cpp</code> installed on your machine:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\"># curl\ncurl -LsSf https://llama.app/install.sh | sh\n\n# powershell\nirm https://llama.app/install.ps1 | iex\n</code></pre>\n<ul>\n<li>Visit <a href=\"https://llama.app\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://llama.app</a> and follow the instructions</li>\n<li>Run with Docker - see our <a href=\"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/blob/master/docs/docker.md\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Docker documentation</a></li>\n<li>Download pre-built binaries from the <a href=\"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/releases\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">releases page</a></li>\n<li>Build from source by cloning this repository - check out <a href=\"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/blob/master/docs/build.md\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">our build guide</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Once installed:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-sh\"># Download and run a model directly from Hugging Face\nllama cli -hf ggml-org/Qwen3.5-0.8B-GGUF\n\n# Launch OpenAI-compatible API server\nllama serve -hf ggml-org/Qwen3.5-0.8B-GGUF\n</code></pre>\n<table>\n    <tr>\n        <td align=\"center\">\n            <img src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/88726b48-1713-48aa-a525-95a02e78afc4\" alt=\"VLM session with `llama cli`\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1310\" height=\"888\" />\n            <i>VLM session with <b>llama cli</b></i>\n        </td>\n        <td align=\"center\">\n            <img src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b402f972-2e32-4def-8771-8d849f08cf2e\" alt=\"Llama Chat, the built-in chat app, against `llama serve` running Qwen 3.6\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1392\" height=\"958\" />\n            <i>Llama Chat, the built-in chat app, against <b>llama serve</b></i>\n        </td>\n    </tr>\n<table></table></table>",
